    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87-a5">

                <pb facs="0218" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg124"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 652.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Rodrigues to
                        Señor Irigoyen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Public Works</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-05-07"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 7,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Señor</hi>:</p>
                <p>I have the pleasure to reply to your courteous note addressed to me yesterday,
                    informing me that the contract for a line of steamers to do service between
                    Panama and San Francisco, Cal., touching at the principal intermediate ports,
                    made between the Government of this Republic and yourself in union with Don José
                    A. March, has been transferred to the Marquis do Campo, a Spanish subject
                    residing in Madrid.</p>
                <p>The very recommendable conditions of the Marquis de Campo and the desire, as you
                    intimate that animates him to draw closer day by day the commercial relations
                    between these Republics and Spain, are, in effect, a guaranty for the stability
                    of this new line of steamers, which will count upon the support that the
                    Executive can give it within the limits of his attributions.</p>
                <p>In these terms the President has instructed me to reply to you, and to manifest
                    at the same time his appreciation of your congratulations, addressed to the
                    Government, on account of the good effect this enterprise is bound to have upon
                    the agricultural and commercial interests of the country.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan J.
                    Rodrigues.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
